[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Escaped Space
Comment=Backslash-s is a string-value escape for a space, and the specification
Comment[x-note]=says that escape runs BEFORE the Exec quoting rule. So an unquoted
Comment[x-note2]=backslash-s really does split the argument in two. This fixture pins
Comment[x-note3]=that ordering; it is deliberately counter-intuitive.
Exec=/usr/bin/spacer one\stwo "three\sfour"
Icon=escaped-space
Terminal=false
